title: Proposition 33
---
order: 33
---
short_label: XI.33
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
----
statement: Similar parallelepipedal solids are to one another in the triplicate ratio of their corresponding sides.
----
----
proof:

Let {AB|sAB} and {CD|sCD} be similar parallelepipedal solids, and let {AE} be the side corresponding to {CF}.

I say that the solid {AB|sAB} has to the solid {CD|sCD} the ratio triplicate of that which {AE} has to {CF}.

Produce {EK}, {EL}, and {EM} in a straight line with {AE}, {GE}, and {HE}. Make {EK} equal to {CF}, {EL} equal to {FN}, and {EM} equal to {FR}. Complete the parallelogram {KL|pKL} and the solid {KP|sKP}. [!just I.3; I.31]

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="500" height="350" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="XI.33 diagram" src="propXI33.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's figure: the similar solids CD and AB, the solid KP built at E
    // on EK, EL, EM equal to CF, FN, FR, and the solids EO and LQ completed
    // on GK and KL with the height of AB.
    //
    // Added, all transparent unless noted: faceless hexagons on the solids'
    // outlines (sAB, sCD, sKP, sEO, sLQ) to carry the solid's highlight,
    // since a polyhedron draws none; faceless quadrilaterals for the
    // parallelograms the proof names (pKL, pCN, pKM, pCR, pEP, pDF, pGK,
    // pAG, pQE), since a filled face would be raised over the figure (#140);
    // the sides AE, CF, GE, HE, FN, FR. EK, EL, jK and HQ are solid slide
    // twins over edges of Joyce's faces, hidden at rest (initiallyHidden),
    // so they can be drawn as the construction reaches them. The angles
    // KEL, AEG, CFN are markers, hidden at rest.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): C0, C3 (off-canvas), C, F,
    // N, R, d (unlettered), H, all on the given solids. Every other point
    // is derived and listed per slide.
