              highlighted: ["angAEG","angCFN"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "angAEG", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "therefore the parallelogram {KL|pKL} equals and is similar to the parallelogram {CN|pCN}.",
              visible: KPd,
              highlighted: ["pKL","pCN"] },
            { text: "For the same reason the parallelogram {KM|pKM} equals and is similar to {CR|pCR},",
              visible: KPd,
              highlighted: ["pKM","pCR"] },
            { text: "and {EP|pEP} equals and is similar to {DF|pDF}.",
              visible: KPd,
              highlighted: ["pEP","pDF"] },
            { text: "Therefore three parallelograms of the solid {KP|sKP} equal and are similar to three parallelograms of the solid {CD|sCD}.",
              visible: KPd,
              highlighted: ["pKL","pKM","pEP","pCN","pCR","pDF"] },
            { text: "But the former three parallelograms equal and are similar to their opposites,",
              visible: KPd,
              highlighted: ["sKP"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "opposite planes equal", ref: "XI.24" }] },
            { text: "and the latter three equal and are similar to their opposites,",
              visible: KPd,
              highlighted: ["sCD"] },
            { text: "therefore the whole solid {KP|sKP} equals and is similar to the whole solid {CD|sCD}.",
              visible: KPd,
              highlighted: ["sKP","sCD"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "solid KP = solid CD", ref: "XI.Def.10" }] },
            { text: "Complete the parallelogram {GK|pGK},",
              visible: GKd,
              highlighted: ["pGK"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "Gj", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "jK", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "parallels completing GK", ref: "I.31" }] },
            { text: "and complete the solids {EO|sEO} and {LQ|sLQ} on the parallelograms {GK|pGK} and {KL|pKL} as bases",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["sEO","sLQ","pGK","pKL"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "KjOQ", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outline },
                  { elem: "BO", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "HQ", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "HQlk", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outline },
                  { elem: "kL", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "lg", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] } },
            { text: "with the same height as that of {AB|sAB}.",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["sAB","HE"] },
            { text: "Then since the solids {AB|sAB} and {CD|sCD} are similar,",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["sAB","sCD"] },
            { text: "therefore {AE} is to {CF} as {EG|GE} is to {FN}, and as {EH|HE} is to {FR}.",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["AE","CF","GE","FN","HE","FR"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AE : CF = EG : FN = EH : FR", ref: "XI.Def.9" }] },
            { text: "And {CF} equals {EK}, {FN} equals {EL}, and {FR} equals {EM},",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["CF","EK","FN","EL","FR","EM"] },
            { text: "therefore {AE} is to {EK} as {GE} is to {EL}, and as {HE} is to {EM}.",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["AE","EK","GE","EL","HE","EM"] },
            { text: "But {AE} is to {EK} as {AG|pAG} is to the parallelogram {GK|pGK},",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["AE","EK","pAG","pGK"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AE : EK = AG : GK", ref: "VI.1" }] },
            { text: "therefore {GE} is to {EL} as {GK|pGK} is to {KL|pKL},",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["GE","EL","pGK","pKL"] },
            { text: "and {HE} is to {EM} as {QE|pQE} is to {KM|pKM}.",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["HE","EM","pQE","pKM"] },
            { text: "Therefore the parallelogram {AG|pAG} is to {GK|pGK} as {GK|pGK} to is {KL|pKL}, and as {QE|pQE} is to {KM|pKM}.",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["pAG","pGK","pKL","pQE","pKM"] },
            { text: "But {AG|pAG} is to {GK|pGK} as the solid {AB|sAB} is to the solid {EO|sEO},",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["pAG","pGK","sAB","sEO"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AG : GK = solid AB : solid EO", ref: "XI.32" }] },
            { text: "{GK|pGK} is to {KL|pKL} as the solid {OE|sEO} is to the solid {QL|sLQ},",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["pGK","pKL","sEO","sLQ"] },
            { text: "and {QE|pQE} is to {KM|pKM} as the solid {QL|sLQ} is to the solid {KP|sKP},",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["pQE","pKM","sLQ","sKP"] },
            { text: "therefore the solid {AB|sAB} is to {EO|sEO} as {EO|sEO} is to {QL|sLQ}, and as {QL|sLQ} is to {KP|sKP}.",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["sAB","sEO","sLQ","sKP"] },
            { text: "But, if four magnitudes are continuously proportional,",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["sAB","sEO","sLQ","sKP"] },
            { text: "then the first has to the fourth the ratio triplicate of that which it has to the second,",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["sAB","sKP"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "triplicate ratio", ref: "V.Def.10" }] },
            { text: "therefore the solid {AB|sAB} has to {KP|sKP} the ratio triplicate of that which {AB|sAB} has to {EO|sEO}.",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["sAB","sKP","sEO"] },
            { text: "But {AB|sAB} is to {EO|sEO} as the parallelogram {AG|pAG} is to {GK|pGK},",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["sAB","sEO","pAG","pGK"] },
            { text: "and as the straight line {AE} is to {EK},",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["AE","EK"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AG : GK = AE : EK", ref: "VI.1" }] },
            { text: "hence the solid {AB|sAB} also has to {KP|sKP} the ratio triplicate of that which {AE} has to {EK}.",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["sAB","sKP","AE","EK"] },
            { text: "But the solid {KP|sKP} equals the solid {CD|sCD}, and the straight line {EK} equals {CF},",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["sKP","sCD","EK","CF"] },
            { text: "therefore the solid {AB|sAB} has also to the solid {CD|sCD} the ratio triplicate",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["sAB","sCD"] },
            { text: "of that which the corresponding side of it, {AE}, has to the corresponding side {CF}.",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["AE","CF"] },
            { text: "Therefore, similar parallelepipedal solids are to one another in the triplicate ratio of their corresponding sides.",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["sAB","sCD"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "XI.33") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "I.3":       "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI3/",
        "I.31":      "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI31/",
        "V.Def.10":  "/elements/books/bookV/definitions/defV10/",
        "VI.1":      "/elements/books/bookVI/propositions/propVI1/",
        "XI.24":     "/elements/books/bookXI/propositions/propXI24/",
        "XI.32":     "/elements/books/bookXI/propositions/propXI32/",
        "XI.Def.9":  "/elements/books/bookXI/definitions/defXI9/",
        "XI.Def.10": "/elements/books/bookXI/definitions/defXI10/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

Now, since the two sides {KE|EK} and {EL} equal the two sides {CF} and {FN}, while the angle {KEL|angKEL} equals the angle {CFN|angCFN}, for the angle {AEG|angAEG} also equals the angle {CFN|angCFN} because {AB|sAB} and {CD|sCD} are similar solids, therefore the parallelogram {KL|pKL} equals and is similar to the parallelogram {CN|pCN}. For the same reason the parallelogram {KM|pKM} equals and is similar to {CR|pCR}, and {EP|pEP} equals and is similar to {DF|pDF}.

Therefore three parallelograms of the solid {KP|sKP} equal and are similar to three parallelograms of the solid {CD|sCD}. But the former three parallelograms equal and are similar to their opposites, and the latter three equal and are similar to their opposites, therefore the whole solid {KP|sKP} equals and is similar to the whole solid {CD|sCD}. [!just XI.24; XI.Def.10]

Complete the parallelogram {GK|pGK}, and complete the solids {EO|sEO} and {LQ|sLQ} on the parallelograms {GK|pGK} and {KL|pKL} as bases with the same height as that of {AB|sAB}. [!just I.31]

Then since the solids {AB|sAB} and {CD|sCD} are similar, therefore {AE} is to {CF} as {EG|GE} is to {FN}, and as {EH|HE} is to {FR}. And {CF} equals {EK}, {FN} equals {EL}, and {FR} equals {EM}, therefore {AE} is to {EK} as {GE} is to {EL}, and as {HE} is to {EM}. [!just XI.Def.9]

But {AE} is to {EK} as {AG|pAG} is to the parallelogram {GK|pGK}, therefore {GE} is to {EL} as {GK|pGK} is to {KL|pKL}, and {HE} is to {EM} as {QE|pQE} is to {KM|pKM}. Therefore the parallelogram {AG|pAG} is to {GK|pGK} as {GK|pGK} to is {KL|pKL}, and as {QE|pQE} is to {KM|pKM}. [!just VI.1]

But {AG|pAG} is to {GK|pGK} as the solid {AB|sAB} is to the solid {EO|sEO}, {GK|pGK} is to {KL|pKL} as the solid {OE|sEO} is to the solid {QL|sLQ}, and {QE|pQE} is to {KM|pKM} as the solid {QL|sLQ} is to the solid {KP|sKP}, therefore the solid {AB|sAB} is to {EO|sEO} as {EO|sEO} is to {QL|sLQ}, and as {QL|sLQ} is to {KP|sKP}. [!just XI.32]

But, if four magnitudes are continuously proportional, then the first has to the fourth the ratio triplicate of that which it has to the second, therefore the solid {AB|sAB} has to {KP|sKP} the ratio triplicate of that which {AB|sAB} has to {EO|sEO}. [!just V.Def.10]

But {AB|sAB} is to {EO|sEO} as the parallelogram {AG|pAG} is to {GK|pGK}, and as the straight line {AE} is to {EK}, hence the solid {AB|sAB} also has to {KP|sKP} the ratio triplicate of that which {AE} has to {EK}. [!just VI.1]

But the solid {KP|sKP} equals the solid {CD|sCD}, and the straight line {EK} equals {CF}, therefore the solid {AB|sAB} has also to the solid {CD|sCD} the ratio triplicate of that which the corresponding side of it, {AE}, has to the corresponding side {CF}.

Therefore, *Similar parallelepipedal solids are to one another in the triplicate ratio of their corresponding sides.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
----
----
guide: This proposition is used in the proof of proposition @XI.37 and later in @XII.8, an analogous proposition about similar pyramids.
#### prop_section ####
kind: corollary
----
toc_summary: If four straight lines are continuously proportional, then the first is to the fourth as a parallelepipedal solid on the first is to the similar and similarly situated parallelepipedal solid on the second, in as much as the first has to the fourth the ratio triplicate of that which it has to the second.
----
----
proof: If four straight lines are continuously proportional, then the first is to the fourth as a parallelepipedal solid on the first is to the similar and similarly situated parallelepipedal solid on the second, in as much as the first has to the fourth the ratio triplicate of that which it has to the second.
